<title>USA: FGIC qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Mesa Unified School District No 4, Ariz., $14.75 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Lake County, Ill., $11 million water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Berkeley County School District, S.C., $9.3 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Beaumont, Texas, $28.88 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Olympia School District No 111, Wash., $23 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Dunn County, Wis., $6.555 million building GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
